  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Moment of inertia of a disc&nbsp;of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;and radius &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&#39; about any of its diameter is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;The moment of inertia of this disc about an axis normal to the disc and passing through a point on its edge will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is ______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ccf6bf2e-3e06-4b7e-9ef2-6a43f12e3956-9896810.PNG\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 140px;\" /></p><p>Given here,&nbsp;</p><p>Moment of inertia of a disc&nbsp;of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;and radius &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&#39; about any of its diameter is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;</p><p>Moment of inertia of disc about centre is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Using parallel axis theorem, we can write</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Hence, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
